# Independent Qwen3.5-4B test lane; baseline cloud lock remains unchanged.
#
# vLLM is a runtime dependency of this lane only. The Qwen2.5-VL-7B lane keeps
# torch 2.7.1 + Transformers 4.57.6 and must never receive this package.
#
# vLLM is pinned to 0.21.0 because it is the last release whose acceleration
# stack targets CUDA 12: it declares a bare `nvidia-cutlass-dsl==4.4.2`.
# From 0.22.1 onward vLLM declares `nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]`, pulling a CUDA 13
# runtime alongside torch's cu126 build. That combination fails at import with
# "libcudart.so.13: cannot open shared object file", because torch==2.11.0+cu126
# ships libcudart.so.12. Kaggle's T4 is SM 7.5 on a CUDA 12 driver, so the CUDA
# 13 line is not usable there regardless of vLLM version.
# vLLM also pins torch==2.11.0 and requires transformers>=4.56, both satisfied.
Pillow==12.3.0
PyYAML==6.0.3
setuptools==78.1.0
torch==2.11.0+cu126
torchvision==0.26.0+cu126
transformers==5.17.0
accelerate==1.12.0
vllm==0.21.0
